OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 413 Thu 19 NovC19:25/52
OL,1,W5j 5Q7k jjs%wsj  w{j#57i         
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%* ** %-,*,$%** %-& (,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSAIrish government denies           
OL,4,A'foot-dragging' over Omagh Bombing     
OL,5,AInquiry                                
OL,7,FJim O'Callaghan, the Irish government's
OL,8,Fjustice minister, said they were fully 
OL,9,Fcooperating with the inquiry and if    
OL,10,Fthere remained unanswered questions "we
OL,11,Fwill certainly look at that".          
OL,13,FNorthern Ireland Secretary Sir Chris   
OL,14,FBryant earlier said it was "almost     
OL,15,Finconceivable" that Ireland would not  
OL,16,Fhold its own inquiry into the bombing. 
